WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.270
Two meadows.

2
00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:04.940
In each, the same four species: buttercup,

3
00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.850
clover, daisy and plantain.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.710
Count the species, and
the meadows tie: 4 each.

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.680
Yet an ecologist would call
one of them far more diverse.

6
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:20.540
If the species are exactly the same, how
can one meadow be far more diverse than

7
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:21.680
the other?

8
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.400
In this mission, you'll meet
biodiversity at three levels:

9
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:28.500
ecosystems, species, and genes.

10
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.850
Then you'll look hard at both meadows,
and find the second thing that species

11
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.780
diversity depends on.

12
00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: explain how two meadows with
the same species can differ in diversity.
